  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data view:** `Kibana Sample Data Logs` (`kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`). The fields that matter here are `response` (with a `response.keyword` subfield for exact matching), `bytes`, `clientip`, `geo.dest`, `extension`, and `url`.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-b5e85409 Web logs overview`** (id `eff-b5e85409-web-logs-overview-e4ec7b8a0dd4`, default time range last 7 days)\n- **Total requests:** metric, count of documents.\n- **Requests over time:** line chart, count per `@timestamp` date histogram.\n- **Responses by status code:** pie chart, count split by `response.keyword`.\n- **5xx responses:** ES|QL metric, `FROM kibana_sample_data_logs | WHERE response.keyword LIKE \"5*\" | STATS server_errors = COUNT(*)`.\n\n**Alert rule: `EFF-b5e85409 5xx spike`** (id `fbe9178e-b082-47b2-a617-d334856107f0`)\n- Rule type `.es-query`, consumer `stackAlerts`, runs every 1m, enabled. Status is `ok`.\n- Counts documents where `response.keyword` matches `5*` in the last 5 minutes, and fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- Tagged `EFF-b5e85409`.\n\n**Choices I made:**\n- The 5xx match uses a wildcard on `response.keyword` rather than an explicit list of codes, so it covers any 5xx code.\n- I did not check the sample data's actual response-code values or time range. The panels will show whatever the data holds, and if the sample data is older than 7 days the dashboard will look empty until the time range is widened.\n- I did not add the rule's actions (no connector was requested), so the rule fires and shows in the Alerts view but sends no notification.\n\n**Environment note:** `KIBANA_TEST_API_KEY` is not set in my shell, so I used the MCP Kibana tools for everything and did not make direct API calls.",
